{%- comment -%}
  sections/hero.liquid
  No template renders this today, the homepage runs hero-slideshow. It
  keeps its preset, though, so it is one click away in the theme editor
  and has to be right the day somebody makes that click. Unlike
  hero-mosaic it has a full set of styles in site.css, so it does work.
{%- endcomment -%}

<section class="hero" data-hero>
  <div class="hero__media">
    {%- comment -%}
      Exactly one image is printed, and it carries the section's only
      fetchpriority. This is a full-bleed photograph sitting behind the
      page heading, so wherever this section is used it is meant to be
      the first thing on the page, which makes it the LCP. There is
      nothing else here worth racing it.

      sizes is 100vw. .hero__media is inset:0 on a full-bleed section,
      so the box IS the viewport. The parallax scales it to between
      1.04 and 1.12, which a browser cannot be told about in sizes and
      which object-fit: cover already over-supplies in almost every
      case, so it is left alone rather than padded with a guess.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if section.settings.hero_image -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The dimensions are the picked image's own. They used to be
        2560x1810 whatever was chosen, which is the Hiran Minar
        photograph's shape: pick a square or a portrait and the browser
        reserved a 1.41:1 letterbox, then shoved the whole page when
        the real thing arrived.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <img src="{{ section.settings.hero_image | image_url: width: 2000 }}"
           srcset="{{ section.settings.hero_image | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w,
                   {{ section.settings.hero_image | image_url: width: 1400 }} 1400w,
                   {{ section.settings.hero_image | image_url: width: 2000 }} 2000w,
                   {{ section.settings.hero_image | image_url: width: 2560 }} 2560w"
           sizes="100vw"
           width="{{ section.settings.hero_image.width }}" height="{{ section.settings.hero_image.height }}"
           fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"
           alt="{{ section.settings.hero_image.alt | escape }}">
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Four candidates off the shipped photograph, the same set
        hero-slideshow draws from. The old pair started at 1280, which
        is 69KB of detail for a 390px phone; the 900 render is 46KB and
        is what most of this traffic will now take. The full 2560 file
        stays at the top of the list for a large or two-times screen.

        width and height stay at the source's 2560x1810 even though src
        points at the 2000 render. They are a ratio, not a promise
        about which file arrives, and 2000x1414 is the same ratio.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <img src="{{ 'hiran-minar-2560-w2000.webp' | asset_url }}"
           srcset="{{ 'hiran-minar-2560-w900.webp' | asset_url }} 900w,
                   {{ 'hiran-minar-2560-w1400.webp' | asset_url }} 1400w,
                   {{ 'hiran-minar-2560-w2000.webp' | asset_url }} 2000w,
                   {{ 'hiran-minar-2560.webp' | asset_url }} 2560w"
           sizes="100vw"
           width="2560" height="1810"
           fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"
           alt="Hiran Minar, Sheikhupura">
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
  <div class="hero__scrim"></div>
  <div class="hero__in">
    <div class="hero__mark">{% render 'kj-mark' %}</div>
    <h1 class="hero__h1">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h1>
    <div class="hero__rule"></div>
    <p class="eyebrow hero__tag">{{ section.settings.tagline }}</p>
  </div>
  <div class="hero__since">{{ section.settings.since_line }}</div>
</section>
{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Hero",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "hero_image", "label": "Hero image (defaults to Hiran Minar photo)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Khan Jee" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "tagline", "label": "Tagline", "default": "House of Brands" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "since_line", "label": "Since line", "default": "Since 1978 · Sheikhupura" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Hero" }]
}
{% endschema %}
